<edge source="china_west_rivalry::vehicle_import_flow" target="bond_market_stress::currency_pressure_index" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">+</data>
  <data key="d29">2</data>
  <data key="d36">0.7</data>
  <data key="d37">A sustained increase in vehicle imports raises demand for foreign currency to pay suppliers and widens the trade deficit, generating immediate depreciation pressure and higher exchange-rate volatility for the domestic currency.</data>
  <data key="d38">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d39">china_west_rivalry</data>
  <data key="d40">bond_market_stress</data>
</edge>
<edge source="china_west_rivalry::vehicle_import_flow" target="global_energy_volatility::oil_price" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">-</data>
  <data key="d29">2</data>
  <data key="d36">0.65</data>
  <data key="d37">An increase in vehicle import flows (notably EVs and efficient models) lowers projected gasoline/diesel demand growth in Europe, reducing near‑term crude demand expectations and exerting downward pressure on oil prices over subsequent quarters.</data>
  <data key="d38">6-18 months</data>
  <data key="d39">china_west_rivalry</data>
  <data key="d40">global_energy_volatility</data>
</edge>
