<edge source="china_west_rivalry::trade_policy_tightness" target="bond_market_stress::cross_border_flows" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">-</data>
  <data key="d29">2</data>
  <data key="d36">0.65</data>
  <data key="d37">Tightened trade measures (tariffs/quotas) raise trade frictions and settlement risk, causing foreign counterparties and investors to scale back portfolio and trade-finance exposures to affected markets, reducing net cross-border capital inflows into fixed-income assets.</data>
  <data key="d38">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d39">china_west_rivalry</data>
  <data key="d40">bond_market_stress</data>
</edge>
<edge source="china_west_rivalry::trade_policy_tightness" target="global_energy_volatility::inflation_expectations" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">+</data>
  <data key="d29">2</data>
  <data key="d36">0.75</data>
  <data key="d37">Tighter trade policies (tariffs/quotas on vehicles and related tech) push up import and component costs, which are quickly transmitted to dealer and input prices and lift market and survey inflation expectations for the coming year.</data>
  <data key="d38">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d39">china_west_rivalry</data>
  <data key="d40">global_energy_volatility</data>
