  <data key="d29">3</data>
  <data key="d36">0.75</data>
  <data key="d37">Sustained higher crude prices raise export revenues and fiscal receipts for energy exporters (notably Russia), directly increasing available funding for fuel, munitions, logistics and troop sustainment and thereby enabling a higher tempo of kinetic operations.</data>
  <data key="d38">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d39">global_energy_volatility</data>
  <data key="d40">russia_ukraine_war</data>
</edge>
<edge source="global_energy_volatility::oil_price" target="russia_ukraine_war::sanctions_enforcement" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">-</data>
  <data key="d29">2</data>
  <data key="d36">0.65</data>
  <data key="d37">Marked oil-price spikes transmit immediate economic pain to sanctioning states and their constituents, creating political pressure to carve exemptions, delay enforcement or tolerate loopholes that reduce the rigor and application of sanctions against energy-linked actors.</data>
  <data key="d38">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d39">global_energy_volatility</data>
  <data key="d40">russia_ukraine_war</data>
</edge>
