  <data key="d34">-</data>
  <data key="d29">3</data>
  <data key="d36">0.8</data>
  <data key="d37">A sustained rise in the policy rate increases real borrowing costs and signals stronger anti-inflation policy, directly lowering market and survey inflation expectations as agents revise demand and wage growth outlooks.</data>
  <data key="d38">6-18 months</data>
  <data key="d39">bond_market_stress</data>
  <data key="d40">global_energy_volatility</data>
</edge>
