  <data key="d29">2</data>
  <data key="d36">0.6</data>
  <data key="d37">Sharp policy rate hikes that provoke domestic economic pain (recessions, higher unemployment) increase political pressure on coalition governments to reallocate spending and reduce foreign commitments, eroding political willingness to sustain coordinated sanctions and military support for Ukraine.</data>
  <data key="d38">6-18 months</data>
  <data key="d39">bond_market_stress</data>
